frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/a6/a60284df5200b84835d261462207e386d975bd4757608919928cabf68623e5fd.png)\n\nWe can break down our division problem as follows:\n\n- Computing $\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}$ means we want to determine how many times $\\frac{5}{6}$ fits into $\\frac{2}{6}.$\n\n- Since both fractions have a *common denominator*, this is the *same* as determining how many times $5$ fits into $2.$\n\n- Therefore, instead of $\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}$, we can simply compute $2÷5.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2÷5=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fae4d19-7336-5557-8df9-bc8e0b6703fa" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Missing Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07add152-5b37-52bd-8854-45d171786094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458630} {:answer/id #uuid "77950df2-d3b5-5fde-85ea-77ce8fd55e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458841} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab618cc-8b04-5be9-9065-aadfcfc094a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458846} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ae5c75-4440-5701-90b6-c15a1adbd97f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459007} {:answer/id #uuid "eb885de0-d8c4-5b37-ab2f-e69a0e7b217a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ab618cc-8b04-5be9-9065-aadfcfc094a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458846} :answer-field/id #uuid "35920fe6-312d-57cd-b63d-a161f2d83b46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab97dcb6-7d97-5f3e-952f-65798b536944" :question/math-academy-id "q-61448" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e69491dc9c333d76a53367a4d12126e2526efbb42f67d17e6b4573788f6f36c.png)\n\nUse the model above to determine the missing number in the equation below.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷\\frac{2}{9}=\\frac{3}{\\boxed{\\,\\,}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The denominators are $3$ and $9.$ We can make a common denominator of $9$ by splitting the shape on the left into $3$ parts vertically: \n\n![](images/64/641525dd15d4739bf548e5cde5e4fbff3b92e3eda3e7af46b0428b22bab1bad0.png)\n\n \n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{9}÷\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n3÷2=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷\\frac{2}{9}=\\frac{3}{\\boxed{\\,2\\,}}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab62b651-0d87-5ed3-b749-11d1e25be6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Fractions Using Models"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eea36d6-2d67-5608-a6f9-ea6518850842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458651} {:answer/id #uuid "20c74a73-779c-5f5a-80c5-75aa843ac875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458691} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf3fcbc-6fcc-5024-977a-13ebce14f693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458745} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb6d24e-2ed4-5b7b-a679-d3d7e0440316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458820} {:answer/id #uuid "f96d4a44-d19b-5e39-a584-9fb139b36540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c74a73-779c-5f5a-80c5-75aa843ac875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458691} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c7d8df2-ef87-51d1-842e-0ca86c1600b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4faa458-b214-58a5-bedf-614e535419db" :question/math-academy-id "q-61602" :question/problem "![](images/28/2891656ddbac17087734ae53802558f71171a2138893995d8fb429dfef3889f8.png)\n\nUse the model above to find the value of $\\frac{2}{3}÷\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominators are $3$ and $6.$ We can make a common denominator of $6.$\n\n We split the shape on the left of the division sign into $2$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](images/8d/8dd0573a6eb88df56d6cec9ef5bd819a429a936609bd51d9fc4ba0e9968e5ef9.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n4÷5=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab62b651-0d87-5ed3-b749-11d1e25be6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Fractions Using Models"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1e0880-1644-5657-9f3e-55b5d7234117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458648} {:answer/id #uuid "1808d9a3-8727-5dee-859e-4864ae5835d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458667} {:answer/id #uuid "352ee3df-51c9-5403-9f7e-63f5a6e86210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458732} {:answer/id #uuid "7a109511-889e-5f0e-b815-5449fcba48d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458845} {:answer/id #uuid "c4378ccf-d537-533b-9b22-ce49ea0c84dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a109511-889e-5f0e-b815-5449fcba48d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458845} :answer-field/id #uuid "c30eda28-7971-561b-964c-bc9fd282c2ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e09f220b-33eb-53ca-b75d-de2074a1fd94" :question/math-academy-id "q-92839" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2ef3a4174cf69597dcbc0e7d403c8fc8c52c8db12a4d2cf3e49c68571888a1d9.png)\n\nFind the value of $\\frac{1}{3}÷\\frac{3}{4}$ given the model above." :question/worked-solution "The denominators are $3$ and $4.$ We can make a common denominator of $3\\times 4=12.$ \n\nWe split the shape on the left of the division sign into $4$ parts vertically, and we split the shape on the right into $3$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](images/07/07693bef459c0417056470494462c411f368f88900d117f48ee155e2c6bba52b.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{12}÷\\frac{9}{12}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n4÷9=\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab62b651-0d87-5ed3-b749-11d1e25be6a8" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Fractions Using Models"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08455ccd-9e2f-5640-a2c5-e4142d78332f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458632} {:answer/id #uuid "3467665d-4fc6-5988-9dd0-690739a0397f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458730} {:answer/id #uuid "6619fb70-a4c9-5861-96ac-dd504b3f7a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458809} {:answer/id #uuid "966dfdc5-de22-590c-99d1-60eece201dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458891} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d0c2e8-fc25-54c1-9309-4423464b87d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "966dfdc5-de22-590c-99d1-60eece201dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458891} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4afafbc-4661-50a1-987d-585c32668b45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14b8de9d-82ba-5f80-a7a7-ca0706d35c9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-92840" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d481b700291d019477ae5ad30a9f647b9ce2a2b5dd9b4fa6b4ab2b5ecebfa43e.png)\n\nFind the value of $\\frac{2}{3}÷\\frac{5}{7}$ given the model above." :question/worked-solution "The denominators are $3$ and $7.$ We can make a common denominator of $3\\times 7=21.$ \n\nWe split the shape on the left of the division sign into $7$ parts vertically, and we split the shape on the right into $3$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](images/d9/d9fdbf9a9f569024446f1be9866d51d32cd77dd69868b6efc30b16a7266abb50.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{21}÷\\frac{15}{21}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n14÷15=\\frac{14}{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷\\frac{5}{7}=\\frac{14}{15}.\n$$"}]}
